    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EKRMVG5VK3JZCPTFZ2\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to create, change, and remove custom subscribe keywords in Klaviyo. </p>\n<p>Custom mobile keywords allow you to better control how you communicate with customers, helping you grow your business while staying true to your brand. Klaviyo allows you to create, change, and remove subscribe keywords for free.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EKWVRWGG71TYMJQ3DV\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>Before learning how to add custom keywords, it is important to know what kind of words can be used. When creating keywords in Klaviyo, follow these guidelines: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Do not use words related to <a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4401822831771\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sex, hate, *alcohol, *firearms, or tobacco (SHAFT)</a>.\n<ul>\n<li>*<a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/17252552814875\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Alcohol and firearms may be allowed with age-gating</a> in certain countries. </li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Use alphanumeric characters (A–Z and 0–9); do not use any other special symbols.</li>\n<li>Keep keywords between 3 and 20 characters.</li>\n<li>Avoid common words that could be used in a normal text conversation, such as “the,” \"that,\" \"are,\" \"can,\" \"here,\" \"about,\" or “and,” which may erroneously subscribe someone who didn’t intend to subscribe.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Note that keywords are not case-sensitive. If you input the keyword as “SHOES,” Klaviyo will accept “shoes,” “Shoes,” etc.</p>\n<p>You can add up to a max of 500 subscribe keywords.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EKTTBS7N4P1J8HSWCK\">Add a custom subscribe keyword</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click your organization name in the lower left corner.</li>\n<li>Navigate to<strong> Settings &gt; SMS &gt; Keyword Responses</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30080348087323\" alt=\"The Keyword Responses tab selected from the left side menu of the SMS setting page.\" width=\"243\" height=\"343\">\n</li>\n<li>Find the <em>Subscribe Keywords </em>section.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30080393382939\" alt=\"Subscribe Keywords section of the Keyword Responses page showing 3 example keywords.\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Add Keyword</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the <em>Create Subscribe Keyword </em>modal, input your keyword.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30080393384219\" alt=\"Create Subscribe Keyword modal showing text boxes where you can add a name, list, and choose double or single opt-in.\">\n</li>\n<li>Choose the list that subscribers who use the keyword should be added to.</li>\n<li>Choose whether you want the keyword to be double or single opt-in.\n<ul>\n<li>(Recommended) Only use single opt-in with tap-to-text, and do not publish single opt-in keywords anywhere on your website. </li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>After adding a keyword, you can use it to trigger a <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115002775172\" target=\"_self\">welcome series</a> or build a flow to<a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001768432\" target=\"_self\"> update the profile properties</a> of those who use the keyword.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EKEZ1HDPYGG7Y14CPJ\">Update a custom keyword</h2>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>You cannot edit the default messages for the opt-out (e.g., STOP) or resubscribe (e.g., UNSTOP) keywords. </p>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li>Click your organization name in the lower left corner.</li>\n<li>Navigate to<strong> Settings &gt; SMS &gt; Keyword Responses</strong>.</li>\n<li>Scroll to the <em>Subscribe Keywords</em> section.</li>\n<li>Find the keyword you want to edit.</li>\n<li>To the right of it, click the 3 dots menu.</li>\n<li>Choose <strong>Edit</strong><strong> Keyword</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the <em>Edit Subscribe Keyword </em>modal, you can change the keyword's:\n<ol>\n<li>Status (i.e., allow customers to subscribe with this keyword or not)</li>\n<li>Name</li>\n<li>List<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28723631902491\" alt=\"Edit Subscribe Keyword menu showing where you can edit an existing keyword's name, submit list, and opt-in process selection.\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong> when you finish making edits.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EK5M0CMGQ1K6PFKMCP\">Delete a custom keyword</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click your organization name in the lower left corner.</li>\n<li>Navigate to<strong> Settings &gt; SMS &gt; Keyword Responses</strong>.</li>\n<li>Scroll to the<em> Subscribe Keywords</em> section.</li>\n<li>Locate the keyword you want to delete.</li>\n<li>Select the 3 dots to the right of your keyword, then click <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>\n<li>In the modal that appears, click <strong>Delete</strong> to confirm that you want to remove the keyword.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28723631880347\" alt=\"Message to confirm that you want to delete a keyword\" width=\"509\" height=\"147\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JCNN5T1E2G7ZNRBC5JY1SVF6\">Using subscribe keywords</h2>\n<p>With subscribe keywords, you can post them on social media, your website, business cards and more. It's a simple and quick way to grow your list, and it's easy to say \"Text JOIN to 123-456-7890.\"</p>\n<p>As you use these keywords, please note that: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>It's important to use disclosure language anywhere you show your subscribe keywords (i.e., on the social media post, website, etc. near the subscribe keyword), so subscribers are informed before they sign up. </li>\n<li>Double opt-in is highly recommended for subscribe keywords. </li>\n<li>If you have multiple sending numbers, remember to change the phone number when you show a subscribe keyword to different countries. </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Note that subscribe keywords are different from compliance keywords (e.g., HELP, STOP, START). Subscribe keywords are an <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/27902671291419\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">opt-in method,</a> while <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360035285472#01H8PSCKC0XVP9F1S1SSVD4JMN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">compliance keywords</a> must, by law, provide certain information or perform a certain action (such as removing SMS consent). </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HQ4009EM29SY8N8YSZ1VFXZE\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360035056972\">Collect SMS subscribers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/29109965092251\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configure when an opt-out keyword removes SMS consent</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360059002271\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Guide to SMS conversations in Klaviyo</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
